    "text": "Video diffusion models have a denoising loop that does not provide scalable serial compute, creating a mismatch with tasks requiring growing serial computation known as the seriality gap.",
    "topic": "Seriality Gap in Video Diffusion Models"
  },
  {
    "text": "For deterministic video prediction, denoising steps in video diffusion models do not add serial computation beyond the backbone, indicating a structural obstacle for handling serial reasoning and simulation tasks.",
    "topic": "Seriality Gap in Video Diffusion Models"
  },
  {
    "text": "The key-value cache in attention mechanisms for autoregressive decoding in video diffusion models grows linearly with context length, leading to memory and bandwidth bottlenecks.",
    "topic": "Memory Bottlenecks in Video Diffusion Models"
  },
  {
    "text": "Existing eviction methods for the key-value cache in video diffusion models poorly track future token utility, exacerbating memory and bandwidth limitations.",
    "topic": "Memory Bottlenecks in Video Diffusion Models"
  },
  {
    "text": "Recent video reconstruction from sparse event streams often suffers from blurred textures and poor long-term stability, while few-step autoregressive video generation accumulates errors and weakens motion dynamics over extended sequences.",
    "topic": "Temporal Artifacts in Video Reconstruction"
  }
